# Line endings, pinned deliberately.
#
# core.autocrlf is true in this clone, so a file authored with CRLF can be
# committed with CRLF. tools/pre-commit and tools/pre-push are `#!/bin/sh`
# scripts, and a CRLF shebang fails on Linux and macOS with
# `bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M` — which would silently disable the guard that
# stops locked-post plaintext reaching this PUBLIC repo on any non-Windows
# clone. The blobs are LF today; this keeps them that way.
#
# (A push review flagged those blobs as already CRLF. They were not — that was
# a `grep -c $'\r'` artifact under MSYS, which counts matching lines oddly and
# reported every line as a hit. Measured on raw bytes, all three are pure LF.
# Use python or `od -c` on `git cat-file blob`, never a shell pipe, to check.)
* text=auto

tools/pre-commit text eol=lf
tools/pre-push   text eol=lf
tools/vault.js   text eol=lf

# Binary: never transform these.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf  binary
*.bin  binary
